^DATABASE = GeoMiame
!Database_name = Gene Expression Omnibus (GEO)
!Database_institute = NCBI NLM NIH
!Database_web_link = http://www.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/geo
!Database_email = geo@ncbi.nlm.nih.gov
^SERIES = GSE288245
!Series_title = Long-term post-ovariectomy mouse model recapitulates hypothalamic transcriptomic changes observed during the menopausal transition in women
!Series_geo_accession = GSE288245
!Series_status = Public on Feb 03 2026
!Series_submission_date = Jan 28 2025
!Series_last_update_date = Feb 03 2026
!Series_summary = Menopause significantly impacts women's health, yet hypothalamic changes during this transition
!Series_summary = remain poorly understood. We analyzed gene expression in human hypothalamic samples across
!Series_summary = menopausal transition, revealing significant changes in inflammatory pathways, KNDy neuron
!Series_summary = signaling, and thermoregulatory genes. This analysis also identified novel central markers of
!Series_summary = menopause, including AKAP5 and CDKN1A (p21). To further investigate these changes, we
!Series_summary = developed a novel mouse model based on long-term (4 months) post-ovariectomy (OVX) that
!Series_summary = mimics the gonadotropin and temperature fluctuations of menopausal transition. Remarkably, the
!Series_summary = posterior hypothalamus of 4-month post-OVX mice closely mirrored the transcriptional changes
!Series_summary = observed in women at the late peri-/early post-menopausal age range (ages 51-55). Both species
!Series_summary = exhibited increased inflammatory signaling and glial activation, alongside altered KNDy neuron
!Series_summary = activity. Our findings provide new insights into the central mechanisms of menopausal symptoms
!Series_summary = and offer a valuable preclinical model for testing interventions.
!Series_overall_design = RNA-seq of the posterior hypothalamus and the preoptic area of sham, 14 days post-, and 4 months post-ovariectomy (OVX) samples
!Series_type = Expression profiling by high throughput sequencing
!Series_contributor = Jordana,C,Bloom
!Series_contributor = Victor,M,Navarro
